meta {
  name: Checkout
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/shop/checkout
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{shopToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "expectedTotal": { "amount": "40.00", "currency": "USD" }
  }
}

docs {
  `expectedTotal` is the only money a shop request may carry, and it is a claim about what was
  **displayed** — not an instruction about what to charge. It can cause a refusal and never a
  price.

  A **409 `PRICE_CHANGED`** carries the fresh cart in `details.cart`, because the next thing the
  customer will do is look at what it now costs. Nothing is written: no order, and no invoice
  number drawn from a gapless sequence.

  On success you get **201** and an order that is `PendingPayment` with a pro forma attached.
  Nothing is invoiced until an administrator confirms the money arrived — this system cannot see
  a bank account, and a commercial invoice issued now would say a sale was settled when nobody
  had checked.
}
